.TH SDL_WPRINTF_VARARG_FUNCV 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_WPRINTF_VARARG_FUNCV \- Macro that annotates a va_list function that operates like wprintf.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_WPRINTF_VARARG_FUNCV( fmtargnumber ) /* __attribute__ (( format( __wprintf__, fmtargnumber, 0 ))) */
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If we were to annotate
.BR vfwprintf :

.IP
.EX
int vfwprintf(FILE *f, const wchar_t *fmt, va_list ap) SDL_WPRINTF_VARARG_FUNC(2);
.EE
.PP

This notes that the second parameter should be a wprintf-style format wide string, followed by a va_list\[char46] The compiler or other analysis tools can warn when this doesn\(aqt appear to be the case\[char46]
.PP
On compilers without this annotation mechanism, this is defined to nothing\[char46]
.PP
This can (and should) be used with
.BR SDL_PRINTF_FORMAT_STRING
as well, which between them will cover at least Visual Studio, GCC, and Clang\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

